Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:16:49 +0800
Subject: core/codemode: record the child sessions nested calls drive

A tool called from Code Mode that starts or drives a child session says so the way the
subagent tool does, with sessionID (or sessionIDs) in its progress or result metadata.
The execute call now records those IDs on the nested call's row
(metadata.toolCalls[i].sessionIDs), so clients can show the child sessions under the
Code Mode run. Only session IDs are kept, not the rest of the nested metadata, so the
rows stay small. Nested progress still passes through as before.

Ocelot-Patch: core/codemode-child-sessions

